Grasp: take a fresh candidate from propose_grasps (current pose revision only; never reuse stale IDs). Run pregrasp then approach, then close_gripper(right). If close succeeds, verify_hold(right) and confirm observe().held_by == ['right'] before lifting. If close returns grasp_not_confirmed (no lift happened), read gripper_motor_feedback_rad.right against gripper_open_rad.right. Retry close once only if the motor is still within 0.12 rad of its open endpoint; otherwise open the empty jaw, retreat to the last verified checkpoint, reobserve, and propose candidates excluding prior IDs. Max 3 attempts. Never pregrasp while holding.

Lift only after actual right hold. Start transfer with placement_aware=True, then call advance() repeatedly (max 16) until done=True. Do NOT call finish_transfer after a successful transfer. Require observe().held_by == ['left'] afterward. If advance fails with dual_hold_not_confirmed or receiver_hold_not_confirmed while the donor right still holds, reobserve and stop for review or perform the documented left-close recovery (close LEFT at the aligned receiver pose, verify both holds, finish_transfer, then place); do not restart the handover from that state (start_collision observed). Unknown collision, IK, or terminal failures stop with no blind retry.

Place: start_place (requires left-only hold), advance until done (max 16). Finish by verifying held_by is empty. Use only current observations; last_failure is historical and does not by itself block recovery.

Limitations: expert evidence is human-engineered corrections from a fixed-rule comparator, not independent discovery. Two prior model continuations failed API contracts (for example, handover retry and recovery paths were not validated), so this code is not verified against the live runtime. Retain this caveat when reusing it."}
